※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=3041

※ A lambda that brings nothing in is written with no list at all, so an empty
※ one would be a second spelling of that.  Where two ways of writing something
※ would mean the same thing in every respect, the language admits one of them.

@[startup, impure]
fn main() → u6:
    let f: fn(u8) → u8 = λ a: u8 [] → u8 { a }
    0u6
